From fe6d28e49ced110a5e2908334c935a78f69239c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:42:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add --frame-packing option to emit the frame packing
 arrangement SEI

x265 defined the SEI payload type FRAME_PACKING but had no way to write it,
so an HEVC encode of side-by-side or top-and-bottom 3D video could not carry
the in-stream mark that players and 3D televisions read (see #970).

--frame-packing <integer> takes the values H.265 defines in Table D.8:
3 side by side, 4 top and bottom, 5 temporal interleaving. It is disabled
by default and the bitstream does not change without it. As x264 does,
frame 0 is signalled as the left view (content_interpretation_type 1).
The message follows H.265 D.2.16 and is written as a prefix SEI with each
IRAP picture (types 3 and 4, persistence flag set) or with every picture
(type 5, where current_frame_is_frame0_flag alternates and the persistence
flag is clear).

X265_BUILD is incremented as x265_param gets a new member.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
